      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stratford%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Norton's manager Walter Colton named the new town after Stratford Hall, the childhood home of Robert E. Lee in Virginia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stratford%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Stratford in 1900, marking the town’s growing importance in the region.",
